      "description": "Objective\nUsing the Magento sample product extract (SFCC-29), investigate whether Zimmermann's existing product hierarchy in Magento maps cleanly to the SFCC master → variation group → variant model, and document any gaps or transformations required before SFCC-25 (Product Type and Variation Model) is configured.\nDocumentation here on Confluence: \nProduct Hierarchy - Adobe SFCC - Confluence\nBackground\nSFCC uses a strict three-level product hierarchy:\nMaster product\n — shared attributes (name, style code, description); not purchasable\nVariation group\n — groups variants by colour; holds colour-level attributes and images\nVariant (SKU)\n — purchasable unit; unique colour + size combination with its own price and inventory\nBefore configuring this model in BM (SFCC-25), we need to confirm that Magento's product structure can be mapped to it — or identify where custom transformation logic will be needed.\nTasks\nExtract and review a representative sample of products from Magento (see SFCC-29)\nMap Magento product attributes to the SFCC three-level hierarchy\nIdentify any structural mismatches (e.g. flat product structure, missing colour/size grouping, non-standard variant logic)\nDocument any transformation or custom logic required to fit Magento data into the SFCC model\nFlag any attributes present in Magento that have no equivalent in the SFCC attribute schema (SFCC-26)\nDefinition of Done\nA documented mapping (or gap analysis) is produced and reviewed, confirming whether SFCC-25 can proceed as-is or whether the story needs updating before configuration begins.",
