      "id": "18213",
      "key": "SFCC-128",
      "summary": "Spike: Familiarise with SFCC GitHub Repo & Review Cartridges (Global-e, Avalara)",
      "description": "Objective\n:\nThe team to familiarise themselves with the SFCC GitHub repository structure, with a focus on the existing cartridges — in particular the Global-e and Avalara cartridges — to understand how they are configured, how they integrate with the platform, and what customisation may be required.\n\n\n\n\nBackground\n:\nThe SFCC repo contains a number of pre-built and third-party cartridges that will form the foundation of the build. Before development begins in earnest, the team needs a working understanding of what is already in place, how the cartridges are wired together, and where configuration changes will be needed.\nVictor and Gids to lead this review with the broader squad.\n\n\n\n\nTasks:\nClone and review the SFCC GitHub repository structure\nIdentify all cartridges present and document their purpose\nReview the Global-e cartridge in detail: configuration files, site preferences, integration hooks, and checkout handoff logic\nReview the Avalara cartridge in detail: configuration files, tax calculation hooks, and storefront-level settings\nDocument any gaps, missing configuration, or customisation required for Zimmermann's setup\nShare findings with the squad as a brief walkthrough or written summary\nDefinition of Done:\nA summary of the repository structure and cartridge inventory is documented, with specific notes on the Global-e and Avalara cartridges covering current state, required configuration, and any open questions.",
